  "note": "Verso body page, single column (prose measure x 0.314-0.904). Two stacked worked-example panels, blocks n=2 (Example 1.2) and n=3 (Example 1.3), each built the same way as p007's: a #dbdcde grey interior flanked by solid cyan #00adef bars. On this verso the WIDE label bar carrying 'EXAMPLE 1.2' / 'EXAMPLE 1.3' in white sideways type is on the LEFT (x 0.262-0.304) and the thin plain bar on the right (x 0.888-0.902) - the mirror of p007, because the label bar always sits on the OUTER edge. The label bars are given role major_heading and the plain bars decorative_image, as on p007. Panel prose sets about 0.9x body. Block n=6 is the displayed Coulomb's-law equation together with its right-ranged number '(1.1)', which is why its bbox runs to x 0.901. This page also carries a footer_rule: the short dark #221f1f footnote separator at y 0.8903-0.8916 spanning x 0.314-0.510, above the starred footnote (block n=8) set at about 0.85x body. Section heading '1.6 COULOMB'S LAW' (n=4) is grey #6d6e71 at 1.45x body. Folio '10' in a pale cyan box in the outer bottom margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
